.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt LEX 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm lex
.Nd generate a C lexical scanner (bounded POSIX core)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl tv
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a lex specification and writes a C scanner.
The definitions section supports
.Li %{ ... %} ,
name definitions and
.Li %s
inclusive or
.Li %x
exclusive start conditions.
The rules section supports
.Li yylex ,
.Li yytext ,
.Li yyleng ,
.Li BEGIN ,
.Li ECHO
and
.Li yywrap ,
longest match with rule order, quoted strings, character classes, repetitions and
.Li ^
/
.Li $
line context.
The generated scanner uses the host
.Xr regex 3
engine.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t
Write the scanner to standard output instead of
.Pa lex.yy.c .
.It Fl v
Report the output path on standard error.
.It Fl o Ar file
Write to
.Ar file .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width lex.yy.c
.It Pa lex.yy.c
Default output.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr yacc 1 ,
.Xr regex 3
.Sh BUGS
Trailing context, the
.Li <<EOF>>
rule, GNU
.Li %option ,
.Li REJECT ,
.Li yyless ,
.Li unput
and
.Li input
are not supported.
The generated scanner reads its input into memory and does not support NUL bytes.
